0..63 Comment "//! An occurrence names an atom inside its binding abstraction."
64..67 Comment "//!"
68..145 Comment "//! The occurrence has a depth below its binder. Admission re-mints each atom"
146..166 Comment "//! with its binder."
167..170 Comment "//!"
171..248 Comment "//! A rule that names its restricted channel is independent of atom spelling."
249..323 Comment "//! A freshness condition limits a rule to permitted instances. The kernel"
324..402 Comment "//! counts each binder above an occurrence. The checker uses that count during"
403..482 Comment "//! matching and critical-pair analysis. Each theory normalizes a process where"
483..502 Comment "//! its rules meet."
503..506 Comment "//!"
507..569 Comment "//! - owes: #1934 — a rule matching a variable both under an"
570..601 Comment "//!   abstraction and beside it"
602..677 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/desc/atom-occurrence.gandr` — that rule, refused"
678..731 Comment "//! - cites: [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting], § 2"
732..808 Comment "//! - cites: [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science], § 4"
809..868 Comment "//! - cites: [Milner-1999-communicating_and_mobile_systems]"
869..943 Comment "//! - cites: [Mayr-1998-higher_order_rewrite_systems_and_their_confluence]"
944..1023 Comment "//! - cites: [Miller-1991-a_logic_programming_language_with_lambda_abstraction]"
1024..1027 Comment "//!"
1028..1151 Comment "//! [Fernandez-2007-nominal_rewriting]: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2006.12.002 \"Fernández and Gabbay, Nominal rewriting\""
1152..1317 Comment "//! [Pitts-2013-nominal_sets_names_symmetry_computer_science]: https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139084673 \"Pitts, Nominal Sets: Names and Symmetry in Computer Science\""
1318..1470 Comment "//! [Milner-1999-communicating_and_mobile_systems]: https://openlibrary.org/works/OL7950513W \"Milner, Communicating and Mobile Systems: the π-Calculus\""
1471..1652 Comment "//! [Mayr-1998-higher_order_rewrite_systems_and_their_confluence]: https://doi.org/10.1016/S0304-3975(97)00143-6 \"Mayr and Nipkow, Higher-order rewrite systems and their confluence\""
1653..1870 Comment "//! [Miller-1991-a_logic_programming_language_with_lambda_abstraction]: https://doi.org/10.1093/logcom/1.4.497 \"Miller, A Logic Programming Language with Lambda-Abstraction, Function Variables, and Simple Unification\""
